    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The test passes. `bin/e2e` ran the full pipeline (build \u2192 start \u2192 Playwright), so the front-end build (which includes the route-tree generation and TypeScript compile) succeeded and the app served the new routes correctly.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change \u2014 **\"when I open a client, show me the projects I'm doing for them\"** \u2014 is implemented as small, additive files following the app's slot/route conventions. The data model already supported it (`project.client_id` exists since `V3`, and `/api/projects` already returns `clientId`), so no migration or new endpoint was needed \u2014 the panel reuses the existing `['projects']` query and filters by client, exactly as `InvoicesPanel` filters by project.\n\nNew files:\n- `slots/defs/clientDetail.ts` \u2014 declares the client-detail slot region.\n- `slots/defs/clientRowActions.ts` \u2014 declares a per-row action region for the clients table.\n- `routes/clients.tsx` \u2014 one-line `<Outlet />` layout route for the `/clients` section (rule 1).\n- `routes/clients.$clientId.tsx` \u2014 the client-detail child route (drilling in is a route, not a flag), rendering `<ClientDetail.Slot>`.\n- `features/clients/open.slot.tsx` \u2014 fills the row-actions slot with the `client-open-<id>` link.\n- `features/projects/ClientProjectsPanel.tsx` \u2014 the projects listing scoped to one client, rendering `client-projects-table` and reusing the `project-row-<id>` / `project-name` anchors.\n- `features/projects/clientProjects.slot.tsx` \u2014 the projects feature filling the client-detail slot (mirrors invoices filling project-detail).\n\nOne minimal edit to `features/clients/ClientsPage.tsx`: added the row-actions slot region (`<ClientRowActions.Slot clientId={c.id} />`) to each row \u2014 the \"add the region and render it\" case rule 3 explicitly allows, matching how `ProjectsPage` already renders `ProjectRowActions.Slot`. Features stay decoupled, sharing only the `['projects']` query key and the `client.detail` / `client.row.actions` slot ids.\n\nAll existing `data-testid`s are preserved; the new ones (`client-open-<id>`, `client-detail`, `client-projects-table`) match the spec.",
